          "content": "Before reading lesson 1, sketch the specimen or experiment. Label axes and state whether your variables are energetic, volumetric, areal, temporal or geometric. Identify one observable that you could record directly, one quantity that requires a model to infer, and one missing process variable. A useful figure has units and a declared temperature; an energy-level sketch should distinguish applied bias from equilibrium. Keep the same conventions throughout the unit and revisit them in the integrated investigation.",
